{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1176043-shield-mechanics-in-w20","id":1176043,"title":"Shield Mechanics in W20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-14T13:24:47-08:00","id":1176043,"title":"Shield Mechanics in W20","content":"How do work shields in W20? <br /> <br /> Help the parry only? <br /> Add absortions dices? <br /> Or increases the difficulty to be attacked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T15:27:46-08:00","id":1176086,"title":"","content":"W20 doesn't include shield rules. M20 and DAV20 both do, but with different rules.<br /> <br /> The M20 rules are more complicated, but are probably better for handling a modern day game where humans have access to things like riot and ballistic shields, but werewolves might be using an ancient shield Fetish that's made of natural materials. The complexity lets it handle a greater range of types. The DAV20 are simpler though, and those might be better if you just want to have some rules and move on.<br /> <br /> The basics:<br /> <br /> M20 shields increase the difficulty to attack you in close combat, but can impart penalties beyond using up a hand. They act as armor against ranged attacks. They do not modify parry difficulties, but do let you parry things you might not otherwise.<br /> <br /> DAV20 shields and defensive weapons (like parrying daggers) modifier both the difficulty to attack you in close combat, and your parry difficulty in close combat, as well as allowing shields to parry ranged attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T04:07:33-08:00","id":1176239,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The Dark Ages has... well, not exactly <i>rules</i> for shields, per se, but mentions them on page 171. Basically, there are two types of shield. One gives an opponent a +1 difficulty to attack rolls, and the other a +2. Nothing is mentioned as to a Dex penalty for the user. The passage mainly focuses on reasons why Garou shun shields -- basically because werewolves are generally powerful enough to reduce most shields to splinters with a single blow, or simply reach around them with their long arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T22:18:29-08:00","id":1176465,"title":"","content":"Dark ages Vampire rules work pretty well for melee and arrows/thrown weapons, but you would probably have to look at how much &quot;soak&quot; it would give to slow down a bullet heading your way, or how much of a beating it can take against fomori, or fellow lupines... I mean Werewolves.<br /> Totally not a Vampire player here.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:49:15-08:00","id":1176933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1176043-shield-mechanics-in-w20?p=1176086#post1176086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 doesn't include shield rules. M20 and DAV20 both do, but with different rules.<br /> <br /> The M20 rules are more complicated, but are probably better for handling a modern day game where humans have access to things like riot and ballistic shields, but werewolves might be using an ancient shield Fetish that's made of natural materials. The complexity lets it handle a greater range of types. The DAV20 are simpler though, and those might be better if you just want to have some rules and move on.<br /> <br /> The basics:<br /> <br /> M20 shields increase the difficulty to attack you in close combat, but can impart penalties beyond using up a hand. They act as armor against ranged attacks. They do not modify parry difficulties, but do let you parry things you might not otherwise.<br /> <br /> DAV20 shields and defensive weapons (like parrying daggers) modifier both the difficulty to attack you in close combat, and your parry difficulty in close combat, as well as allowing shields to parry ranged attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the exposure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you all for your help. Now I have a clear idea of how to implement the shields in my game. \\o/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}